  "notes": "Official cause code left TBD/provisional per FORM-366 fields; narrative provides detailed root-cause discussion (actuator transition point shift from April 2023 maintenance) but no coded cause category was assigned in block 13 (empty) or the cause_code field. Two parallel failure chains: (1) CV stall -> scram -> Group II isolation; (2) sensed MSL flow transient -> Group I isolation/MSIV closure -- both stem from the same test evolution but are physically distinct causal paths, modeled separately per rule 5. HPCI was placed in service to control pressure but did not inject; included as involved system, not as a backup with a stated inoperability window to link BACKED_UP_BY. No manufacturer, EIIS-coded breaker/component details, or previous-similar-event LER number provided in narrative (section present but empty) -- no stub LER emitted."
